Z||000002||Eric||06-29-2000||10:20 PM||||Did you use a DA on the bumpers?  Did you stop sanding and start spraying on the first picture or did you sand all the rest of those spots out first?  I've got to repaint mine too and I was wondering the best way to get them cleaned up.  I've stripped and sanded, but I'm no where near as far as you are in your first picture.  Hey, that car looks damn good too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bill Osmer||06-29-2000||10:23 PM||||Great job!<P>Sure wish I could paint like that - is the bottom "black" as shiny as it appears or is it just flash from the camera?<P>Did you clear-coat it, too?<P>Bill||||reg||14
Z||000004||BOILERMAKER||06-29-2000||10:51 PM||||Yes, I did use a DA on the bumpers (actually on everything, but the rest of the car didn't need nearly as much attention as the hood, front bumper, and rear bumper).  I basically left it right where you saw it in the first picture.  Sure, I touched it up a bit, but when sanding, you are mainly looking for everything to be even.  <P>So, when you have a pit (formerly known as a rock chip ... which was my biggest problem on the front fascia) you want it to be even with the rest of the front. When sanding, you focus on that pit, but you don't want to make a groove to replace the pit, so you focus and then broadly sand around it, focus, and broadly sand, etc until you have the pit out and have what I had on the front bumper (please notice that I had lots of pits).  This way the transition is from top coat through the coats finally to the center of the attention that was previously the pit.<P>Yes, the black is as shiny as in the picture.  The black and the gold (champaign gold to be exact) were all clear coated (3 coats if I'm not mistaken).<P>I'd have to set you up with my dad, Scott, as far as a paint job goes.  He's a master at the paint, but the real key is the body work.  Lousy body work makes for a lousy paint job.  If you get closer you can see where I should have spent more time on it, but I won't make that same mistake twice on the black one.||||reg||1
